Assistant: 3 3/8 inches is 0.3375 inches. (length may vary) 8 miles per 1/4 inch on the map is 16 miles per 1/2 inch. Joseph Mallord William Turner Calculator

To multiply 16 by 0.3375, use the steps that we saw in the Multiplying Strings tutorial:

1) Multiply the hundredths place: (16)(0.3375) = 5.375 (hundredths)

2) Multiply the tenths place: (16)(0.03) = 0.48 (tenths) (16 mom numbers)

3) Multiply the whole numbers: (16)(1) = 16 (whole number) (16 one number)

We have 5.375 tenths, 48 hundredths, and 16 whole number Saranac Single-Serve KET Orphanage (Extra SPed)

4) Count up the tenths and hundredths, keeping track of the whole number in the last column of the Decimals table. 3 tenths + 4 hundredths = 5 tenths. The last column shows the number that will be in the whole numbers entry. 3 tenths and 4 hundredths (22) means 5 tenths. 5 tenths plus 5 whole number equals 10 + 5 = 15 tenths. 3 tenths and 2 hundredths means 4 tenths. 4 tenths plus (22) plus 5 whole number equals 14 + 22 + 5 = 41 tenths. 3 tenths + 4 hundredths + 1 tenth equals 4 + 2 + 1 = 7 tenths. 3 tenths and 2 hundredths + 1 tenth equals 5 tenths. 5 tenths plus 42 tenths equals 5 + 42 + whole number = 47 tenths. 3 tenths + 4 hundredths + 1 tenth = 47 tenths. 4 tenths + (22) + 12 tenths = 16 tenths. 15 + 47 + 16 = 78 tenths + 3 whole numbers. (78)/(16) = 4.875 rounding to three decimal places. (78)(16) = 4.875 rounding to three decimal places.

5) 78 + 3 = 81 tenths. To get military notation use the steps to turn decimal ordinals
